    <string name="cfg_guardian">Guardian</string>
    <string name="cfg_guardian_text">While an alarm rings, Guardian blocks Settings (force stop, uninstall), the notification shade and the power menu, and sends you back to the alarm. Calls and emergency calls are never blocked. It does nothing when no alarm rings.</string>
    <string name="cfg_guardian_restricted">App installed outside the Play Store, Android 13+: if the switch is greyed out, try to turn it on once, then open App info → ⋮ → Allow restricted settings and come back.</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_title">Restricted settings</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_desc">NightLatch is installed outside the Play Store, so Android blocks some settings until you unlock them by hand: Guardian (accessibility) and, from Android 15, Display over other apps.\nIf a switch is greyed out or Android says “Restricted setting”:\n1. Try to turn it on once: Android shows the block and unlocks the option below.\n2. Tap OPEN APP INFO, then ⋮ (top right) → Allow restricted settings, and confirm with your PIN or fingerprint.\n3. Come back here and turn it on.</string>
